# Fast English Podcast — production secrets/tuning environment template.
#
# This file documents VARIABLE NAMES ONLY. The real file lives on the server at
#   /opt/fast-english/shared/secrets/pocketbase.env
# owned by root:root with mode 0600, and is NEVER committed to Git.
#
# Mandatory (set before `install.sh` / `deploy.sh` can configure services):
# FEP_SUPERUSER_EMAIL=admin@example.com
# FEP_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD=change-me-32-chars-min
#
# Optional — settings encryption (recommended): random 32-char string.
# The production systemd unit always passes `serve --encryptionEnv=
# PB_ENCRYPTION_KEY`; with this variable set, the app settings (incl. any
# SMTP/S3 credentials) are stored encrypted in pb_data. Without it PocketBase
# starts with settings stored unencrypted (verified 0.39.9). Set it BEFORE
# the first `configure.sh` run so credentials are encrypted from the start.
# PB_ENCRYPTION_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# Optional — SMTP. Leave unset for the honest disabled state
# (smtp.enabled=false; no transactional email in production until approved).
# FEP_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# FEP_SMTP_PORT=587
# FEP_SMTP_USERNAME=...
# FEP_SMTP_PASSWORD=...
# FEP_SMTP_TLS=true
#
# Optional — S3-compatible backup bucket (only when approved).
# Uses the dedicated backups bucket; never the file-storage bucket.
# FEP_BACKUP_S3_ENABLED=true
# FEP_BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=fast-english-backups
# FEP_BACKUP_S3_REGION=us-east-1
# FEP_BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.example.com
# FEP_BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY=...
# FEP_BACKUP_S3_SECRET_KEY=...
# FEP_BACKUP_S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
#
# Optional — production smoke tests (dedicated disposable accounts only).
# smoke-prod.sh generates its own disposable Student accounts; only the
# Staff account used by the payment-review smoke is configured here (must
# be an active, verified staff_admins account created through
# `pnpm staff:bootstrap`).
# FEP_SMOKE_STAFF_EMAIL=staff@example.com
# FEP_SMOKE_STAFF_PASSWORD=...
#
# Staff bootstrap + legacy diagnostic (values stay OUTSIDE Git):
# FEP_PB_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
# FEP_PB_SUPERUSER_EMAIL=...
# FEP_PB_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD=...
# FEP_STAFF_EMAIL=...
# FEP_STAFF_PASSWORD=...
# FEP_STAFF_DISPLAY_NAME=...
#
# Never put real customer data or other secrets in this file beyond the
# variables above. Rotate any leaked value immediately.
